final: also silence GCC 16's -Wuninitialized around the pugixml include

The unity translation unit already wraps pugixml.cpp in a pragma ignoring
-Wmaybe-uninitialized for a known false positive in the document-move code.
GCC 16 reports the same diagnostic as the definite -Wuninitialized:

    pugixml.cpp:491:66: error: ...xml_node_struct::header is used uninitialized
      [-Werror=uninitialized]
    pugixml.cpp:7688:55: note: in expansion of macro PUGI_IMPL_GETPAGE
      new (other) impl::xml_document_struct(PUGI_IMPL_GETPAGE(other));

other->header is valid there: it is read to compute the argument for the
placement new that replaces the object.  Add -Wuninitialized to the pragma.
The standalone compile of pugixml.cpp (regular builds) is unaffected.

diff --git a/src/psymp3.final.cpp b/src/psymp3.final.cpp
index 4aac1a48..e8c881ce 100644
--- a/src/psymp3.final.cpp
+++ b/src/psymp3.final.cpp
@@ -47,9 +47,13 @@
 // code when the unity TU gives it extra inlining context; the standalone
 // compile of the same file is clean. Clang has no such warning group and
 // would fail the pragma itself under -Werror=unknown-warning-option.
+// GCC 16 reports the same false positive in xml_document::_move -- reading
+// other->header to build the placement-new argument -- as the definite
+// -Wuninitialized, so silence that group too.
 #if defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__)
 #pragma GCC diagnostic push
 #pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wmaybe-uninitialized"
+#pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wuninitialized"
 #endif
 #include "../third_party/pugixml/pugixml.cpp"
 #if defined(__GNUC__) && !defined(__clang__)
